Distributed RAG Scraper Framework
Author

Noura S. Al Hassanieh

1. Introduction

The objective of this project is to design and implement a Distributed Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Scraper Framework capable of collecting information from websites, storing the extracted content, performing semantic search, and generating answers using a language model.

The framework integrates web scraping, distributed processing, vector search, and question-answering technologies into a single system. The implementation uses Scrapy and Playwright for data collection, Redis and Celery for distributed processing, PostgreSQL for metadata storage, Qdrant for vector search, SentenceTransformer for embeddings, and FLAN-T5 for answer generation.

2. System Architecture

The system consists of the following components:

FastAPI Backend
Scrapy Crawlers
Playwright
Redis
Celery Workers
PostgreSQL
Qdrant
SentenceTransformer
FLAN-T5

diagrams/Architecture Diagram.png.png
Figure 1. Architecture of the Distributed RAG Scraper Framework.

The FastAPI backend serves API requests and communicates with the vector database and language model. Redis acts as a task broker, while Celery executes scraping tasks. Scrapy and Playwright collect data from websites. PostgreSQL stores metadata and Qdrant stores vector embeddings used for semantic retrieval.

