The /rag endpoint successfully returned answers together with supporting sources.



10. Challenges and Solutions
Docker Dependency Conflicts

During backend containerization, dependency conflicts involving qdrant-client and related packages were encountered. Docker Compose and infrastructure services were successfully deployed while backend image troubleshooting was performed.

Hugging Face Model Integration

FLAN-T5 required downloading and configuration before successful integration into the RAG pipeline.

API Development

Several endpoint and configuration issues were resolved through testing using Swagger UI.

11. Conclusion

A Distributed Retrieval-Augmented Generation Scraper Framework was successfully designed and implemented.

The framework integrates:

Scrapy
Playwright
Redis
Celery
PostgreSQL
Qdrant
FastAPI
SentenceTransformer
FLAN-T5

The system supports web scraping, semantic search, vector retrieval, and retrieval-augmented question answering with source attribution. The final implementation demonstrates a complete pipeline from data collection to AI-powered answer generation.